<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="theme-color" content="#142238"><title>About | Sherubtse Lost &amp; Found</title><link rel="icon" href="/Sherubtse_logo/images.jpg"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css"><script src="/js/app.js" defer></script></head><body><header class="site-header"><nav class="nav-wrap" aria-label="Main navigation"><a class="brand" href="/"><img src="/Sherubtse_logo/images.jpg" alt="Sherubtse College crest"><span><strong>Sherubtse</strong><small>Lost &amp; Found</small></span></a><button class="menu-toggle" aria-label="Open menu" aria-expanded="false">☰</button><div class="nav-links"><a href="/">Home</a><a href="/browse">Browse items</a><a href="/report-lost">Report lost</a><a href="/report-found">Report found</a><a href="/my-items" data-auth-link hidden>My posts</a><a class="active" href="/about">About</a></div><div class="nav-account" data-account></div></nav></header><main class="page-main about-page">
<section class="about-hero"><div><span class="eyebrow eyebrow-dark">Our campus. Our community.</span><h1>Small acts of care.<br>A big difference.</h1><p>A misplaced notebook, a forgotten bag, a set of keys. Behind every lost item is a student hoping to find it again. This board helps Sherubtse students take the next step together.</p><a class="button button-gold" href="/browse">Find an item</a></div><img src="/Sherubtse_logo/images.jpg" alt="Sherubtse College crest"></section>
<section class="about-story"><span class="eyebrow eyebrow-dark">Why this board exists</span><h2>One place to look. One way to help.</h2><p>Lost belongings can interrupt a busy college day. This student community project brings lost and found reports into one searchable space, making it easier to connect the person who found an item with the person looking for it.</p><p>Posting is for Sherubtse student accounts with an eight-digit student number and its matching college email. Anyone can browse the board. This is a community project; reports are submitted by students and are not independently verified by the college.</p></section>
<section class="about-values" aria-label="Using the board"><article><span class="step-number">01</span><h2>Share a useful report</h2><p>Add the item name, category, location and date. Describe identifying details and include a photo if you have one. Search existing posts before creating another.</p></article><article><span class="step-number">02</span><h2>Connect with care</h2><p>Signed-in students can see the poster's college email. Phone sharing is your choice for each post. Ask for a distinctive detail to confirm ownership and arrange a handover in a public campus place.</p></article><article><span class="step-number">03</span><h2>Bring the story full circle</h2><p>Once an item is reunited with its owner, use My posts to mark it returned or delete the report. Keeping the board current helps everyone find relevant information.</p></article></section>
<section class="about-story safety-note"><h2>A little privacy goes a long way.</h2><p>Never publish passwords, bank details, full ID numbers, or photos that expose private information. Keep some identifying details private so an owner can prove an item is theirs. You can manage lost and found email alerts in your profile.</p></section>
<section class="feedback-section" id="feedback"><div class="feedback-intro"><span class="eyebrow eyebrow-dark">Help shape the board</span><h2>How does it feel<br>to use this space?</h2><p>Tell us what helped, what felt confusing, or what you would like improved. Your experience matters.</p><p class="muted">Feedback is saved privately with your account for the project maintainer. It is not displayed publicly. Please leave out passwords and sensitive personal details. This form is not monitored for urgent requests.</p></div><div><p id="feedback-signin" class="form-notice" hidden>Please <a href="/login">sign in</a> with your student account to share feedback.</p><form id="feedback-form" class="report-panel"><label>How was your experience?<select name="rating" required><option value="">Choose a rating</option><option value="5">5 - Excellent</option><option value="4">4 - Good</option><option value="3">3 - Okay</option><option value="2">2 - Needs improvement</option><option value="1">1 - Difficult</option></select></label><label>Your feedback<textarea name="message" required minlength="10" maxlength="2000" rows="5" placeholder="What worked well? What could be better?"></textarea><small>10 to 2,000 characters.</small></label><button type="submit" class="button button-navy">Share feedback</button><p id="feedback-message" class="form-message" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></form></div></section>
</main><footer class="site-footer"><div><a class="footer-brand" href="/">Sherubtse College Lost &amp; Found</a><p>Kanglung, Trashigang, Bhutan</p></div><div class="footer-links"><a href="/browse">Browse listings</a><a href="/report-lost">Report lost</a></div><small>Student community project · 2026</small></footer></body></html>
